      <activity id="c49c92d2-57fc-50c2-8696-ce19bec67f45" activityNameId="995d044f-c7b4-5706-a93f-fe2228d99a88" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Formic acid from methyl formate, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Formic acid from methyl formate, at plant
The process "formic acid from methyl formate, at plant, RER" is modelled for the production of formic acid from methyl formate in Europe. Raw materials and energy consumptions are modelled with literature data. The emissions are estimated. Infrastructure and transports are calculated with standard values.;
CAS number: 000064-18-6; 
Formula: CH2O; 
Synonyms: methanoic acid; 
UUID: 38527c86-1e16-3ee5-8ae0-1bd0f11113b4
Production of formic acid including materials, energy uses, infrastructure and emissions.
Location: The inventory is modelled for Europe.
Technology: Carbonylation of methanol
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Literature data 
Extrapolations: Transports and emissions are modelled with standard methods.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_38527c86-1e16-3ee5-8ae0-1bd0f11113b4.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
